# LLM Providers (set the one you use)
OPENAI_API_KEY=
GOOGLE_API_KEY=
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
XAI_API_KEY=
DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=
DASHSCOPE_API_KEY=
DASHSCOPE_CN_API_KEY=
ZHIPU_API_KEY=
ZHIPU_CN_API_KEY=
MINIMAX_API_KEY=
MINIMAX_CN_API_KEY=
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
MISTRAL_API_KEY=
MOONSHOT_API_KEY=
GROQ_API_KEY=
NVIDIA_API_KEY=

# SEC EDGAR (US company filings, point-in-time). No key; a contact address SEC can reach you at.
#SEC_EDGAR_USER_AGENT=Your Name your@email.com

# FRED (Federal Reserve macro data). Free key: https://fred.stlouisfed.org/docs/api/api_key.html
#FRED_API_KEY=

# TypeSafe Jev: screens StockTwits and Reddit posts for the Sentiment Analyst. Optional.
#TYPESAFE_API_KEY=
#TYPESAFE_DEFAULT_MODEL=jev-latest

# Custom OpenAI-compatible endpoint (vLLM, LM Studio, llama.cpp). Local servers need no key.
#OPENAI_COMPATIBLE_API_KEY=

# AWS Bedrock (pip install ".[bedrock]"). Bearer token, or the AWS credential chain; set the region either way.
#AWS_BEARER_TOKEN_BEDROCK=
#AWS_DEFAULT_REGION=us-west-2
#AWS_PROFILE=

# Remote Ollama server. Unset uses http://localhost:11434/v1.
#OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://your-ollama-host:11434/v1

# Override these DEFAULT_CONFIG keys. Provider, models, language and round counts also skip their CLI prompt.
#TRADINGAGENTS_LLM_PROVIDER=openai
#TRADINGAGENTS_DEEP_THINK_LLM=gpt-6-sol
#TRADINGAGENTS_QUICK_THINK_LLM=gpt-6-luna
#TRADINGAGENTS_LLM_BACKEND_URL=
# Optional per-model connections: all four Python keys default to None.
# deep_think_llm_provider -> TRADINGAGENTS_DEEP_THINK_LLM_PROVIDER
# quick_think_llm_provider -> TRADINGAGENTS_QUICK_THINK_LLM_PROVIDER
# deep_think_llm_backend_url -> TRADINGAGENTS_DEEP_THINK_LLM_BACKEND_URL
# quick_think_llm_backend_url -> TRADINGAGENTS_QUICK_THINK_LLM_BACKEND_URL
# Each nonempty individual provider/URL wins independently; otherwise inherit
# llm_provider / backend_url. Missing, None and empty strings inherit. A different
# provider STILL inherits the common URL: no compatibility guard or URL repair.
# A URL alone retains the common provider. With neither URL, existing adapter
# defaults, provider ENV and mandatory-URL errors remain. Old connections keep
# their behavior. Azure/Bedrock retain their own endpoint/auth mechanisms;
# these keys do not add generic base-URL support to either adapter.
# Mixed-protocol example (models use the existing ENV keys; no new aliases):
#TRADINGAGENTS_DEEP_THINK_LLM=gpt-5.6
#TRADINGAGENTS_DEEP_THINK_LLM_PROVIDER=openai
#TRADINGAGENTS_DEEP_THINK_LLM_BACKEND_URL=http://localhost:8317/v1
#TRADINGAGENTS_QUICK_THINK_LLM=gemini-3.8-flash-high
#TRADINGAGENTS_QUICK_THINK_LLM_PROVIDER=google
#TRADINGAGENTS_QUICK_THINK_LLM_BACKEND_URL=http://localhost:8317/v1beta
# Explicit URLs avoid inheriting an incompatible common protocol path.
# Auth still uses OPENAI_API_KEY / GOOGLE_API_KEY for this pair, not per-model
# keys. Two endpoints of one provider share its existing auth mechanism.
# OpenCode config is not read; its value "none" does not make Python keyless.
# See README "Per-model provider and URL" for all existing auth ENV names.
#TRADINGAGENTS_OUTPUT_LANGUAGE=English
#TRADINGAGENTS_MAX_DEBATE_ROUNDS=1
#TRADINGAGENTS_MAX_RISK_ROUNDS=1
#TRADINGAGENTS_CHECKPOINT_ENABLED=false

# Paths and alpha benchmark. Unset uses ~/.tradingagents and the regional index.
#TRADINGAGENTS_RESULTS_DIR=
#TRADINGAGENTS_CACHE_DIR=
#TRADINGAGENTS_MEMORY_LOG_PATH=
#TRADINGAGENTS_BENCHMARK_TICKER=SPY

# Lower temperature means less run-to-run variation on models that honor it.
#TRADINGAGENTS_TEMPERATURE=0.0

# Retry budget for every LLM SDK. Raise it to ride out 429 throttling.
#TRADINGAGENTS_LLM_MAX_RETRIES=6

# Cap output tokens to bound a model that runs long and trips a timeout.
#TRADINGAGENTS_MAX_TOKENS=8192

# Independent per-tier reasoning (optional). high/low are illustrative examples,
# not defaults; both Python keys default to None. Leave commented to inherit.
# Python keys: deep_think_reasoning_effort / quick_think_reasoning_effort.
#TRADINGAGENTS_DEEP_THINK_REASONING_EFFORT=high
#TRADINGAGENTS_QUICK_THINK_REASONING_EFFORT=low
# Each tier uses its nonempty setting, then its actual provider's nonempty shared
# setting below. If neither is set, no reasoning parameter is sent, so provider
# defaults apply. Missing keys, None and empty strings mean inheritance, not
# disabling reasoning. The literal string "none" is not an inheritance sentinel;
# whether it is supported depends on the provider/model.
# Partial override example: deep=high, shared OpenAI=medium, quick unset gives
# deep=high and quick=medium.
# Shared fallbacks and adapter parameters: openai_reasoning_effort ->
# reasoning_effort (OpenAI, existing OpenAI-compatible providers and Azure),
# anthropic_effort -> effort (Anthropic),
# google_thinking_level -> thinking_level (Google). Valid values depend on the
# provider/model, not a universal enum; high/low do not work for every model.
# Compatibility change, including old shared settings: no outgoing model-name
# filtering or value rewriting. Nonempty values (including literal none and
# Google minimal, also for Pro) pass unchanged at the application boundary.
# SDK/server acceptance is not guaranteed; errors are not hidden by retrying
# without reasoning. To omit a rejected parameter, remove BOTH the tier value
# and its provider's shared fallback. This is not a universal server-side off
# switch. Bedrock gains no new reasoning protocol. Response normalization,
# DeepSeek reasoning round-trip and MiniMax reasoning/text separation stay intact.
# These settings do not change models, agent assignments, provider, endpoint,
# or other generation settings. See README "Per-tier reasoning effort".
# Shared provider-specific reasoning/thinking depth (optional; examples only).
# In the CLI, the shared choice is a fallback; tier overrides survive. No new
# per-tier menus are added. Existing prompt-skip rules remain: a nonempty provider
# env var or matching shared reasoning env var skips the shared prompt; the two
# tier overrides alone do not.
#TRADINGAGENTS_OPENAI_REASONING_EFFORT=medium
#TRADINGAGENTS_GOOGLE_THINKING_LEVEL=high
#TRADINGAGENTS_ANTHROPIC_EFFORT=high
